<div class="page">
<header class="masthead">
<p class="eyebrow">explorations/reviews/skills-review-style.md · 2026-10-08</p>
<h1>How you review a skill</h1>
<p class="standfirst">A Sonnet archaeology of your 68 comments in 35 threads on the skills review page (10-05 to 10-08) and the chat that followed. The profile in part 3 is what a rewriting workflow would apply to the re
</header>
<nav class="parts" aria-label="Parts"><h2>Four parts</h2><ol>
<li><a href="#part1">The fourteen lenses</a></li><li><a href="#part2">The twelve moves beyond the text</a></li><li><a href="#part3">The profile</a></li><li><a href="#part4">Where the evidence is thin</a></li></ol></nav>
<section id="part1" class="part"><h2><span class="num">1</span>The fourteen lenses</h2>
<p>A lens is a question you ask of a sentence, a rule or a list. Lenses 1 to 8 are the ones on file from 10-05 and 10-06; 9 to 14 are new, from 10-07 and 10-08.</p>
<ul><li>Lens 1. Can a newcomer decode every word?</li><li>Lens 2. Can the agent act on it?</li><li>Lens 3. Does it agree with the rest of the skill and with his positions?</li><li>Lens 4. Does the reader need it here? Wh
<section id="part2" class="part"><h2><span class="num">2</span>The twelve moves beyond the text</h2>
<p>Where a comment on wording led you to fix the process underneath. The note gives each move's trigger and what it became.</p>
<ul><li>M1. A rewrite of the section, not a patch of the line.</li><li>M2. A separate writer.</li><li>M3. Archaeology of what workers actually did.</li><li>M4. A cold read, and routing.</li><li>M5. A rename at the source
<section id="part3" class="part"><h2><span class="num">3</span>The profile</h2>
<p>Use the curator's terms. Apply the fourteen lenses (the eight on file, and lenses 9 to 14 above) to the whole skill at once. Do not wait for a comment.</p>
<h3>Set the reader and the register</h3>
<ol>
<li value="1">The reader is a novice to the repository, which every agent is. The curator judges with human eyes, often on a phone, without the record in mind. Explain every internal reference or remove it. Work on the w
<li value="2">Write about halfway toward ASD-STE100. Describe first, in short sentences. Then give the procedure, with one instruction in each sentence, in the imperative, with the condition first.</li>
<li value="3">State rules positively. Use "do not" only where no positive instruction says the same.</li>

